  "verbalization": "Stipuleanoside R2 is shown to interact with CD276 antigen through multiple pathways, with SK-OV-3 cells acting as a common target in all three evidence chains. The drug is implicated in targeting SK-OV-3, which is known to be a target of Glaucolide B, (2R)-2-bromo-2-iodoacetic acid, and ent-Eusynstyelamide B. These compounds all direct their activity toward CD276 antigen, suggesting a shared mechanism of action involving the CD276 antigen. The evidence supports a potential role for Stipuleanoside R2 in modulating CD276 antigen expression or function, possibly through the inhibition of downstream targets like SK-OV-3. The high scores in all three paths indicate a strong, consistent relationship, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The presence of multiple targets and their shared effect on CD276 antigen suggests a possible network of interactions, but the core mechanism remains under investigation.",
